  "step_3": "The decision reason requires calculating an aspiration level as the mean of all outcomes (1633.33) and then comparing the probabilities of exceeding this level. However, the individual does not reference any such benchmark or perform any calculation resembling an average of outcomes. Instead, the individual focuses on the marginal differences in probabilities for specific monetary outcomes (0€ and 100€ more), which reflects a different type of reasoning—possibly focusing on regret, disappointment, or marginal gains—rather than aspiration-level comparisons. There is no indication that the individual computed or used the mean of outcomes, nor that they assessed which lottery gives a higher chance of surpassing a derived reference point. The information considered (small probability differences on specific outcomes) and the justification (trade-off between slightly better gain and slightly higher risk of nothing) do not align with the aspiration-level rule. Therefore, it is unlikely the individual used this specific decision reason.",
